Hi @Marc_Laboulais and @Miroslav_Gluch,

I have the same device so I started to play with the code and I found a workaround:

in com.tuya.zigbee/drivers/lcdtemphumidsensor/device.js you have to comment out this section (with /* and */):

/*
                if (this.isFirstInit()){
                        await this.configureAttributeReporting([
                                {
                                        endpointId: 1,
                                        cluster: CLUSTER.POWER_CONFIGURATION,
                                        attributeName: 'batteryPercentageRemaining',
                                        minInterval: 65535,
                                        maxInterval: 0,
                                        minChange: 1,
                                }
                        ]);
                }
*/

And then it will initialize OK and after a while it will report humidity, temperature and battery status.

Hope this will help you.

